" Written by the Arch OS Installer. Vim's own defaults.vim first - a vimrc of
" one's own switches them off otherwise - and then what makes it read like any
" other editor. `:help option-list` names everything that can go here.
unlet! skip_defaults_vim
source $VIMRUNTIME/defaults.vim

set number
set laststatus=2

" Four spaces for a tab, and a search that ignores case until it holds a
" capital letter, lit up where it matched.
set expandtab shiftwidth=4 softtabstop=4
set ignorecase smartcase hlsearch

" Vim's own dark scheme of muted greys and blues, close to the Nord the console
" and the prompt are drawn in.
colorscheme habamax
